</name><name><surname>Hudis</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Winer</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Cohen</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Wheeler</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Norton</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Adjuvant chemotherapy in older and younger women with lymph node positive breast cancer</article-title><source>JAMA</source><year>2005</year><volume>293</volume><fpage>1073</fpage><lpage>1081</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'JAMA||293|1073||bib5|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15741529</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib6"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mustacchi</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Milani</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Pluchinotta</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>De Matteis</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Rubagotti</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Perrota</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Tamoxifen or surgery plus tamoxifen as primary treatment for elderly patients with operable breast cancer: The G.R.E.T.A. Trial. Group for Research on Endocrine Therapy in the Elderly 3</article-title><source>Anticancer Res</source><year>1994</year><volume>14</volume><fpage>2197</fpage><lpage>2200</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Anticancer Res||14|2197||bib6|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7840523</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib7"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Ottawa</collab></person-group><article-title/><source>Minster of Industry, Statistics Canada. Life Table, Canada, Provinces and Territories, 2000&#x02013;2002</source><year>2006</year>Internet Communication</citation></ref><ref id="bib8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wyld</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Garg</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Kumar</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Brown</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Reed</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Stage and treatment variation with age in postmenopausal women with breast cancer: compliance with guidelines</article-title><source>Br J Cancer</source><year>2004</year><volume>90</volume><fpage>1486</fpage><lpage>1491</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Br J Cancer||90|1486||bib8|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15083173</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wyld</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Reed</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The need for targeted research into breast cancer in the elderly</article-title><source>Br J Surg</source><year>2004</year><volume>90</volume><fpage>388</fpage><lpage>399</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Br J Surg||90|388||bib9|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12673739</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>